## Fix stale references in Claude skills

Context: Review of the project skills (.claude/skills/) surfaced three files
that had drifted from the canonical rules and the real toolchain: the
changelog skill documented a flat changelogs/YYYY-MM-DD.log path while
.cursorrules requires changelogs/v<version>/<user>_<date>.log; the deploy
skill pointed at non-existent paths and a non-existent deploy-prod target;
the ai-feature skill referenced renamed plugin skills and a hardcoded
user-local path.

Changes:

1. .claude/skills/changelog/SKILL.md
   Path convention corrected to changelogs/vX.Y.Z/<github-user>_YYYY-MM-DD.log
   with the version taken from pyproject.toml (matches .cursorrules).
2. .claude/skills/deploy/SKILL.md
   Fixed docs/deployment.md and scripts/deploy.config.sh paths, replaced the
   non-existent databricks-authentication skill reference with
   databricks-core/databricks-setup-local, and removed the contradictory
   make deploy-prod suggestion from the release flow.
3. .claude/skills/ai-feature/SKILL.md
   Corrected plugin skill names (databricks-synthetic-data-gen,
   databricks-mlflow-evaluation), dropped a hardcoded /Users/... path and a
   non-existent agent-evaluation skill, and updated the stale "5 agents,
   zero eval coverage" premise to the current 10-agent, partial-coverage
   reality.

Modified files:
- .claude/skills/changelog/SKILL.md
- .claude/skills/deploy/SKILL.md
- .claude/skills/ai-feature/SKILL.md
- changelogs/v0.9.2/alexxx-db_2026-11-12.log

