## Least-privilege grants: superuser opt-in + schema-scoped UC readback

Context: regulated-industry posture — provisioning previously granted
DATABRICKS_SUPERUSER to every workspace admin (Postgres superuser bypasses
all schema ACLs) and the UC readback grant was catalog-wide ALL_PRIVILEGES.
Both are now narrow-by-default with deliberate opt-ins for the broad paths.

Changes:

1. LakebaseGraphProvisioner + provision_steps (src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/)
   New grant_superusers flag (default False). The "superusers" task step and
   _step_grant_superuser_to_managers only run when the caller opts in via the
   provision payload. Individual operators can still be promoted on demand
   through the existing lakebase-grant-superuser settings action.

2. grant_uc_catalog (src/back/core/databricks/lakebase/grants.py)
   New uc_schema parameter. When set, grants USE_CATALOG on the catalog plus
   USE_SCHEMA,SELECT on <catalog>.<schema> (covers all current+future synced
   tables) instead of catalog-wide ALL_PRIVILEGES — now documented as the
   development-only fallback. Both call sites (graph provisioner, registry
   Bootstrap) pass their schema, so the in-app path is least-privilege by
   default.

3. scripts/bootstrap/lakebase-perms.sh
   New -S/--uc-schema flag selecting the same least-privilege grant shape;
   -c without -S keeps the catalog-wide ALL_PRIVILEGES shortcut with an
   explicit "dev shortcut" message.

4. databricks.yml
   Hardcoded "group_name: users" on both app ACLs replaced with
   ${var.app_access_group} (default "users") so regulated installs can scope
   app access to a real group via --var or deploy.config.sh.

5. Settings UI (settings.html + settings.js)
   Provision dialog: UC checkbox label updated to "schema-scoped readback";
   new opt-in checkbox "Promote workspace admins to DATABRICKS_SUPERUSER".

6. search_path hardening
   Schema name now escapes embedded double quotes before interpolation into
   SET search_path in LakebaseConnectionPool, LakebaseFlatStore and
   LakebaseBase (5 sites).

7. docs/deployment.md
   Grant matrix and lakebase-perms.sh section updated: schema-scoped
   USE_CATALOG+USE_SCHEMA,SELECT documented as the production path;
   ALL_PRIVILEGES demoted to a development shortcut for pre-schema deploys.

