## Connection health hardening: SEA poll backoff + idle-conn ping

Context: two scale/reliability items from the Databricks review —
fixed-interval SEA polling generated needless API chatter on long-running
statements, and the Lakebase pool lent silently-dead sockets because
``conn.closed`` only sees locally-observed shutdowns.

Changes:

1. StatementExecutionWarehouse (src/back/core/databricks/)
   Poll interval now doubles from 0.2 s and clamps at 1 s
   (_POLL_INTERVAL_MAX_SECONDS) inside _wait_for_terminal. Short
   statements still finish inside the first fast checks; long-running
   ones settle into a 1 s cadence.

2. LakebaseConnectionPool (src/back/core/databricks/lakebase/)
   Idle entries now carry idle_since; on checkout a connection parked
   longer than POOL_PING_IDLE_S (30 s, in constants.py) is verified with
   SELECT 1 before being lent out. The ping runs outside the pool lock
   (acquire was restructured: pick/reserve under the lock, slow work
   outside it). A failed ping discards the connection and re-enters
   acquire. Both pool consumers (registry + graph) share the fix.

Modified files:
- src/back/core/databricks/StatementExecutionWarehouse.py
- src/back/core/databricks/lakebase/LakebaseConnectionPool.py
- src/back/core/databricks/lakebase/constants.py
- tests/back/core/databricks/test_lakebase_connection_pool.py (new)
- tests/units/core/test_statement_execution_warehouse.py

